WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:06.490
I'm going to suggest to you today that we
start referring to Donald Trump's tariffs

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:11.630
as tax increases on everyday Americans because
that's what they actually are in practice.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:14.599
And that's something I thought that Republicans
claim to be against.

00:00:14.599 --> 00:00:18.280
And I've been talking about this since Donald
Trump's tariffs on China.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.450
We're just an idea now.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:23.800
There are a reality, as I told you in the
last segment, new tariffs have been announced

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.800
on Mexico.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:31.420
Those start at 5% potentially escalating all
the way up to 25% according to Donald Trump.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.370
If you believe that, uh, that is actually
what he is going to do.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.809
Now, it's really important to understand,
and I feel like a broken record with this.

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:43.469
China doesn't pay the tariffs that Donald
Trump placed on them.

00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:49.410
Mexico will not pay the tariffs that Donald
Trump is placing on that is in the process

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.469
of placing on them.

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:59.289
The tariffs on China and Mexico make their
stuff more expensive to import to the United

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:00.289
States.

00:01:00.289 --> 00:01:07.550
So when you import it, you pay China or Mexico
the same amount for their stuff.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:10.800
Plus you pay something to the United States
government.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.910
In addition to that, a tariff, it is effectively,
it is effectively a tax.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:22.430
Trump has said times his tariffs are forcing
China to pay however many billions of dollars.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:23.870
That's just not how it works.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:31.750
If China has a $100 product that the United
States buys and you put a 25% tariff on Chinese

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:37.730
goods, the American company or person who
buys the hundred dollar thing from China is

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:42.460
still paying China, just the a hundred bucks
and then in addition to that, they pay the

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:44.240
US government 25 bucks.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:50.430
In the case of a hypothetical 25% tariff,
what this means is that the American company

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:56.710
or the American person paying the tariff on
the Chinese stuff ends up with $25 that they

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:01.811
could have spent at local businesses, could
have spent in other ways within the American

00:02:01.811 --> 00:02:06.250
economy, but they don't have those 25 bucks
because they paid it to the government as

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.250
a tariff.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:13.340
I thought that small government, low tax conservatives
were against that and they wanted Americans

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:18.439
to keep more of their own money in order to
do whatever they want in order to stimulate

00:02:18.439 --> 00:02:20.079
local business.

00:02:20.079 --> 00:02:22.049
This is bad for the United States.

00:02:22.049 --> 00:02:24.470
This boycott this, I'm sorry.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:33.940
This tariff program is crushing soybean exports,
which are down 97% from 2017 in the United

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.060
States.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:40.780
Trump's tariffs are crushing whiskey exports
because of the retaliatory tariffs that are

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.010
put in place.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:48.200
Whiskey exports down 32% in the fourth quarter
of 2018 compared to the fourth quarter of

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:53.719
